#: ../../../topics/exceptions.rst:6
msgid "Exceptions"
msgstr "例外"

#: ../../../topics/exceptions.rst:8
msgid ""
"Here's a list of all exceptions included in Scrapy and their usage, except "
"for the :ref:`download handler exceptions <download-handlers-exceptions>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.CloseSpider:1
msgid ""
"Raised from a :ref:`spider callback <topics-spiders>` to request the spider "
"to be closed/stopped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.CloseSpider:4
msgid "*reason* is a string with the reason for closing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.CloseSpider:6
msgid "For example:"
msgstr "例如："

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.CloseSpider:8
msgid ""
"def parse_page(self, response):\n"
"    if \"Bandwidth exceeded\" in response.text:\n"
"        raise CloseSpider(\"bandwidth_exceeded\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.DontCloseSpider:1
msgid ""
"Raised in a :signal:`spider_idle` signal handler to prevent the spider from "
"being closed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of scrapy.exceptions.DropItem:1
msgid ""
"Raised from the :meth:`process_item` method of an :ref:`item pipeline "
"<topics-item-pipeline>` to stop the processing of an item."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.IgnoreRequest:1
msgid "Raised to indicate that a request should be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.IgnoreRequest:3
msgid ""
"A :ref:`downloader middleware <topics-downloader-middleware>` can raise it "
"from its :meth:`~scrapy.downloadermiddlewares.DownloaderMiddleware."
"process_request` or :meth:`~scrapy.downloadermiddlewares."
"DownloaderMiddleware.process_response` method to drop a request, and a :"
"signal:`request_scheduled` signal handler can raise it to drop a request "
"before it reaches the :ref:`scheduler <topics-scheduler>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.NotConfigured:1
msgid ""
"Raised by a :ref:`component <topics-components>` from its ``__init__()`` or :"
"meth:`from_crawler` method to indicate that it will remain disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.NotConfigured:4
msgid "Only the following components can be disabled this way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.NotConfigured:6
msgid ":ref:`Downloader middlewares <topics-downloader-middleware>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.NotConfigured:7
msgid ":ref:`Extensions <topics-extensions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.NotConfigured:8
msgid ":ref:`Item pipelines <topics-item-pipeline>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.NotConfigured:9
msgid ":ref:`Spider middlewares <topics-spider-middleware>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.NotSupported:1
msgid "Raised to indicate that a requested feature is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.NotSupported:3
msgid ""
"For example, Scrapy raises it when text-parsing shortcuts such as :meth:"
"`response.css() <scrapy.http.TextResponse.css>` or :meth:`response.xpath() "
"<scrapy.http.TextResponse.xpath>` are used on a :class:`~scrapy.http."
"Response` whose content is not text, or when sending a request whose URL "
"scheme has no matching :ref:`download handler <topics-download-handlers>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.StopDownload:1
msgid ""
"Raised from a :class:`~scrapy.signals.bytes_received` or :class:`~scrapy."
"signals.headers_received` signal handler to :ref:`stop the download <topics-"
"stop-response-download>` of the response body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.StopDownload:5
msgid ""
"The ``fail`` boolean parameter controls which method will handle the "
"resulting response:"
msgstr "``fail`` 布尔参数控制哪个方法会处理结果的响应："

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.StopDownload:8
msgid ""
"If ``fail=True`` (default), the request errback is called. The response "
"object is available as the ``response`` attribute of the ``StopDownload`` "
"exception, which is in turn stored as the ``value`` attribute of the "
"received :class:`~twisted.python.failure.Failure` object. This means that in "
"an errback defined as ``def errback(self, failure)``, the response can be "
"accessed though ``failure.value.response``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.StopDownload:15
msgid "If ``fail=False``, the request callback is called instead."
msgstr "如果``fail=False`` ，请求回调将被调用。"

#: ../../../../scrapy/exceptions.py:docstring of
#: scrapy.exceptions.StopDownload:17
msgid ""
"In both cases, the response could have its body truncated: the body contains "
"all bytes received up until the exception is raised, including the bytes "
"received in the signal handler that raises the exception. Also, the response "
"object is marked with ``\"download_stopped\"`` in its :attr:`~scrapy.http."
"Response.flags` attribute."
msgstr ""

